detaileddescription.para:
A test program uses three classes:

the runner, which reads the command line, runs the suites, and returns the exit code;

the suite, a named group of test cases;

the test_case, a named sequence of checks, made with expect() and require().

The topics are grouped in four parts:

how to write the tests, in C++ API;

how to test C code, in C API;

the macros that enable the framework, in Configuration;

the options of the test programs, in Command-line options.
